---
import { stages } from '../data/stages';
---
<section class="workspace-section" id="workspace">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Your study workspace</p><h2>Keep the thread<br /><em>in your hands.</em></h2></div><p class="section-description">Progress is deliberately simple. Mark stages complete, export your trail, and take it with you when you switch devices.</p></div>
  <div class="workspace-grid">
    <div class="progress-card">
      <div class="workspace-card-top"><span class="mono-label">LOCAL PROGRESS</span><span data-progress-label>0 / {stages.length} complete</span></div>
      <div class="big-progress"><span data-progress-bar></span></div>
      <p data-progress-copy>Nothing is checked off yet. That is a perfectly good place to begin.</p>
      <div class="workspace-actions">
        <button class="small-button" data-export>Export progress</button>
        <label class="small-button small-button-outline">Restore progress<input data-import type="file" accept="application/json" hidden /></label>
        <button class="small-button small-button-quiet" data-reset>Reset</button>
      </div>
      <p class="privacy-note">Export is a readable JSON file. Restore offers Merge or Replace after confirmation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="practice-card"><span class="resource-type">PRACTICE COMPANION</span><h3>One chunk.<br /><em>One honest session.</em></h3><p>Use the full practice system when you want the paper trace, debugging drill, AI prompt, and completion standard for a stage.</p><a class="button button-dark" href="/dsa-for-data-science/practice/">Open practice guide <span>↗</span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
